def max_path_sum(triangle, row, col):
    # Base case: if we've reached the bottom of the triangle
    if row == len(triangle) - 1:
        return triangle[row][col]

    # Recursive case: choose the maximum of the two possible paths from the next row
    return triangle[row][col] + max(max_path_sum(triangle, row + 1, col), max_path_sum(triangle, row + 1, col + 1))
```

